    "accuracy": "Free-weight lifts are the best case for a single camera: the joints that matter are visible and move in a plane the camera can see. Treat the feedback as a second pair of eyes, not a coach: a camera in 2D cannot see rotation or depth, and a lifter in the wrong clothes or light will confuse it."
